WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.640
So the Lux project is an incredible way&nbsp;
to bring together the diverse collections

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.900
across the cultural heritage&nbsp;
units at Yale. It allows us to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.580
fulfill our mission, to steward these&nbsp;
objects forever and for all people&nbsp;. 

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:20.573
You should think of Lux as a doorway. It  is our way&nbsp;
to share the opportunities &nbsp;

00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:22.834
to explore and discover what we have.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:28.449
Lux is revolutionary because it's not&nbsp;
just another database. It uses the same paradigm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:33.463
that major search engines do to connect knowledge&nbsp;
regardless of where that knowledge is from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:38.760
There  are lots of different audiences for Lux and so&nbsp;
when I think about Lux I think of the student here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:48.032
at Yale who will use Lux for reasons of curiosity.
For the visitor Lux is a way to imagine a visit at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:53.001
Yale that would encompass all of the incredible&nbsp;
cultural heritage collections I'm remembering my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.001 --> 00:00:58.931
days when I was a Art History student in New York&nbsp;
working on Charles Sheeler. Had I had Lux 20 years ago

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:06.234
I would have discovered the monographs in the&nbsp;
Haas Arts Library, I would discover the letters, 

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:12.660
the correspondence of Charles Sheeler in the Beinecke&nbsp;
Library,  the objects of the artist Charles Sheeler

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.834
in the Yale University Art Gallery. 

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:17.820
In building Lux we paid particular attention to ensuring

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:24.180
that the application is easy to use by anyone&nbsp;
regardless of age background or any other factor.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.209
So when you log on to Lux you can quickly search&nbsp;
for anything that you're interested in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.209 --> 00:01:35.700
There's a simple search box, put in a word hit Enter. But&nbsp;
you also have the ability to do really complex&nbsp; searches

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.576
 using our advanced search system.

00:01:37.576 --> 00:01:42.567
Each of us comes to the kinds of questions we ask as scholars and researchers

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:46.459
 with a set of biases&nbsp;
and we don't know what we don't know 

00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:52.620
and what Lux can do for anybody regardless of what they're&nbsp;
working on is allow them to see dimensions of an&nbsp;&nbsp;issue,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.380
 a problem,  a topic,  that they just didn't know&nbsp;
existed. So if you get interested in a topic, &nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.720
you're going to be able to explore that. Go down rabbit&nbsp;
holes come out here see something that you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:09.468
never imagined before that changes the way you&nbsp;
think about what you thought you were interested&nbsp;&nbsp;in. 

00:02:09.468 --> 00:02:16.554
Lux is light and we welcome you to use Lux to&nbsp;
discover and to fulfill your curiosity.

00:02:16.554 --> 00:02:31.560
[Music]

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:37.924
[Music Fades]

